# Shell scripts are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows would otherwise land every script CRLF. Git
# Bash tolerates that -- it is patched to ignore a trailing CR -- but WSL bash,
# dash/sh, and Linux CI reading a Windows-authored tree do not. Without this
# rule a project bootstrapped on Windows ships CRLF scripts to all of them, with
# no signal until something outside Git Bash tries to run one.
*.sh text eol=lf
